.ad l
.nh
.SH NAME
md_docs_2RPC \- RPC 
.PP
RPC stands for Remote Procedure Call and is supported in MaxOS in the syscore/ipc/rpc\&.h,\&.cpp files\&. However, calling functions this way between a server and client can be annoying therefore a custom IDL (Interface Descriptor Language) has been implemented\&. To use this place {name}\&.rpc in the library of choice and the buildsystem will autogenerate the stubs for your function, both client and serverside\&.
.PP
Example: 
.PP
.nf
package greeting;
version 1\&.0;
path /greeting/

service greeting_server {

    rpc int64 say_hi(string name);
    rpc (int64, string) compute_answer(uint32 a, uint32 b) [urgent];
    rpc void notify(string message) [oneway];
}

.fi
.PP
.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fCpackage <name>;\fP Defines the group for the services defined in the file
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fCversion <v>;\fP Indicates what spec of the rpc file format this package compiles with
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fCpath <path>;\fP Defines the path to generate the files\&. Header will be placed in 'include/{path}/{name}\&.h' and source files will be placed in 'include/{path}/{name}\&.h'
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fCservice <service_name> { \&.\&.\&. }\fP Defines an endpoint where the specified functions will exist on
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fCrpc <return> <method>(arglist) [flags];\fP Defines an RPC function that can be called
.PP
.PP
When changing the \&.rpc file, make sure to run 'make rpc' to ensure the autogenerated files are updated\&.
.PP
